  "implementation": [
    "Audio callbacks and PCM conversion are nonisolated; checked Sendable Mutex-owned state protects conversion and capture IDs.",
    "A bounded stream permits eight PCM chunks of at most 32 KiB, consumed by one task. Overflow is a terminal capture error.",
    "Typed text and microphone PCM share the same Realtime socket, serialized writer, turn ownership, tool execution and final response path.",
    "Server VAD has automatic response creation and interruption disabled. Only an owned timestamp-validated provider speech event can interrupt work or playback; raw local energy records selection hints only.",
    "Selection history covers at most 10 seconds/512 ranges of forwarded PCM. It resolves speech without a local energy transition and avoids substituting a later selection when provider events are delayed.",
    "Input clears fence old capture IDs and session-relative sample timestamps. Interrupted admitted tools still return their actual terminal result once, without a stale final response.",
    "Audio interruptions, route recovery and media-services reset invalidate obsolete capture and playback ownership."
